.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Private credentials —— never commit/sync (plaintext secrets)
.claude/cic_login.local.md

# Runtime hook log —— accretes local no-chat-text breach events; not source.
# The .tmp* sibling is the atomic-rewrite staging file used when the log is
# pruned; a hard crash mid-prune can leave one behind, and a stray temp must
# never surface as an untracked change.
cscpt/.clint.log
cscpt/.clint.log.tmp*

# dlint runtime state —— local, machine-specific, never source.
#   .dlint_receipts.jsonl : which files FULL dlint has linted, and at what
#                           content hash. Written by dlint.py, read by
#                           dlint_quick.py's deliverable gate. Machine-local by
#                           nature (absolute paths), and a stale copy from
#                           another machine would silently vouch for a file
#                           never linted here.
#   .dlint.log            : per-invocation trace, so "the hook never fired"
#                           stays distinguishable from "it fired and found
#                           nothing" (cp/ccsim/hook_guide.md §7.7).
#   .dlint_state/         : per-session markers —— which deliverables still owe
#                           a FULL lint, and which files have been reminded.
# The .tmp* siblings are atomic-rewrite staging files; a hard crash mid-prune
# can leave one behind, and a stray temp must never surface as untracked.
# The `.elint*` names are the retired spelling of the same three, kept ignored
# so a machine still carrying them does not surface them as untracked.
cscpt/.dlint_receipts.jsonl
cscpt/.dlint_receipts.jsonl.tmp*
cscpt/.dlint.log
cscpt/.dlint.log.tmp*
cscpt/.dlint_state/

# alint runtime log —— one line per invocation of the TEA1 in-flight gate, so
# "the hook never fired" stays distinguishable from "it fired and found
# nothing" (cp/ccsim/hook_guide.md §7.7). Local trace, never source; the .tmp*
# sibling is the atomic-rewrite staging file a prune may leave behind.
cscpt/.alint.log
cscpt/.alint.log.tmp*

# hlint runtime log —— one line per UserPromptSubmit invocation (stage +
# trigger names), for the same §7.7 reason as the two above. Added after a
# missed `#trigger` was blamed on the hook never firing, when in fact it had
# fired and named the right file; the log makes that answerable by `grep`
# instead of by excavating session transcripts.
cscpt/.hlint.log
cscpt/.hlint.log.tmp*

# post_compact runtime log —— one line per PostCompact invocation. This one is
# not merely useful, it is the ONLY evidence the hook exists: PostCompact's
# output reaches the user and never the model or the transcript, so before this
# log existed "did it fire?" was unanswerable, and the hook sat dead for 70 days
# whilst looking registered and healthy. See `cp/ccsim/hook_guide.md` §6.9.
cscpt/.post_compact.log
cscpt/.post_compact.log.tmp*

# pre_compact runtime log —— one line per PreCompact invocation, for the same
# §7.7 reason as the logs above: an empty file is equally consistent with "clean
# session" and "the harness never called it". Overridable via
# CCSIM_PRE_COMPACT_LOG. Local trace, never a source of truth; the .tmp* sibling
# is the atomic-rewrite staging file a prune may leave behind.
# NOT here on purpose: `cscpt/.plint_state/`. plint's state is tempdir-based BY
# DESIGN —— its own docstring says a dot-file beside the script "would show up in
# git status … and eventually be committed or tidied away". A stanza would hide
# the very drift that directory's existence is meant to reveal, so if it appears
# again, VOID it and find what set PLINT_STATE_DIR to a repo path.
cscpt/.pre_compact.log
cscpt/.pre_compact.log.tmp*

# mlint runtime log —— one line per Stop invocation of the `#m2` sprint gate.
# Same §7.7 reason as the three above, PLUS one this file alone has: the log is
# also mlint's per-prompt LEDGER, the guard that stops a blocking Stop hook
# firing twice for the same prompt. Deleting it therefore re-arms one block per
# prompt already blocked —— harmless, but not merely a lost trace. The .tmp*
# sibling is the atomic-rewrite staging file a prune may leave behind.
cscpt/.mlint.log
cscpt/.mlint.log.tmp*

# tlint runtime log —— one line per invocation of the time-integrity lint, on
# BOTH its events. Same §7.7 reason as the four above: a lint that logs only
# breaches leaves an empty file, and an empty file is equally consistent with
# "clean session" and "the harness never called it". This one is pure trace ——
# nothing reads it back —— so deleting it costs only history. The .tmp* sibling
# is the atomic-rewrite staging file a prune may leave behind.
cscpt/.tlint.log
cscpt/.tlint.log.tmp*
# blint runtime log —— one line per invocation across its FOUR stages
# (PostToolBatch corrector, mark_chapter guard pre/post, prompt reset), for
# the same hook_guide §7.7 reason as the logs above: a hook that leaves no
# trace is how PostCompact sat dead 70 days. This one is ALSO two ledgers in
# one —— the `corrected:*@hash` lines are the mid-turn corrector's dedup
# ledger, and `marker_recorded`/`prompt_reset` are the marker guard's state.
# Deleting it costs one duplicate advisory and disarms the marker guard until
# the next marker (fail-open by design) —— never a loop, never a false deny.
# The .tmp* sibling is the atomic-rewrite staging file a prune may leave
# behind. (Voided `❌_` files are NEVER gitignored —— user ruling; nothing in
# this stanza touches that.)
cscpt/.blint.log
cscpt/.blint.log.tmp*
